  "notes": "CONJUGATION: Godan る-verb. {断|た}ち{切|き}る → {断|た}ち{切|き}って → {断|た}ち{切|き}った.\n\nUSAGE: A compound of {断|た}つ (to sever) + {切|き}る (to cut). The figurative sense (sense 2) is extremely common and often used for ending relationships, breaking habits, or stopping negative cycles.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {縁|えん}を{断|た}ち{切|き}る: to sever ties\n- {未練|みれん}を{断|た}ち{切|き}る: to cut lingering attachments\n- {連鎖|れんさ}を{断|た}ち{切|き}る: to break a chain/cycle\n- {悪循環|あくじゅんかん}を{断|た}ち{切|き}る: to break a vicious cycle",
